    "original_review_scope_verbatim": "Complete original main Theorem 6.5 and its full classification proof. The author’s introduction explicitly calls complete classification of invariant curves the main accomplishment. Its actual required core is retained: brane/bow and fixed-point setup, tangent-weight formula and proof, compact butterfly surgery, two novel noncompact constructions, Young-diagram/BCT reformulations, curve-pencil generation and both column-imbalance cases. Every original author-coded colored diagram remains editable TikZ. Later example classifications and the following compactness corollary are excluded; no intermediate lemma adds a separate count. The pencil-operator Greek Gamma macro is rendered as the same upright mathop Gamma to avoid a fontspec null-glyph mapping from the upstream DeclareMathOperator macro; literal pen uses are unchanged.\n\nNo mathematical refereeing or assistant-generated proof. Native source and corresponding saved publisher PDF are hash-bound. Fresh two-pass XeLaTeX completed with the actual project .tex-cache TEXMF and -no-shell-escape. Both passes exit0; final log has no undefined references/citations, missing glyphs, or overfull boxes. Author-coded diagrams retained and rendered. Selected theorem, proof formulas, core construction and compatibility glyphs were compared with original publisher PDF. No mathematical-truth review or model proof.\n\nFont compatibility: original pencil Greek-Gamma operator is rendered as mathop Gamma with unchanged pen uses, fixing fontspec mapping to missing U+0000. Its visible Gamma, subscript and spacing were compared with publisher p.16. Corollary6.7 is resolved as a precise forward source reference; it is not invoked by the selected classification proof.\n",
